  "captions": [
    {
      "start": 60.5,
      "end": 63.05,
      "text": "Around ten thousand years ago, sea levels"
    },
    {
      "start": 63.05,
      "end": 65.63,
      "text": "rose and the Arctic coastline moved."
    },
    {
      "start": 66.02,
      "end": 69.21,
      "text": "A population of mammoths became isolated on"
    },
    {
      "start": 69.21,
      "end": 72.17,
      "text": "Wrangel Island, with no easy route back"
    },
    {
      "start": 72.17,
      "end": 74.39,
      "text": "to the mainland. They survived there for"
    },
    {
      "start": 74.39,
      "end": 77.16,
      "text": "thousands of years, among the last mammoths"
    },
    {
      "start": 77.16,
      "end": 80.77,
      "text": "on Earth.  Other populations disappeared earlier, and"
    },
    {
      "start": 80.77,
      "end": 83.9,
      "text": "differently. Mammoths on the East European plains"
    },
    {
      "start": 84.17,
      "end": 86.77,
      "text": "vanished roughly fifteen thousand years ago."
    },
    {
      "start": 87.2,
      "end": 88.64,
      "text": "The population on St."
    },
    {
      "start": 88.96,
      "end": 91.54,
      "text": "Paul Island in Alaska lasted until about"
    },
    {
      "start": 91.54,
      "end": 93.09,
      "text": "fifty six hundred years ago."
    },
    {
      "start": 93.39,
      "end": 95.87,
      "text": "Studies of their remains found changes in"
    },
    {
      "start": 95.87,
      "end": 99.26,
      "text": "isotope signatures toward the end, consistent with"
    },
    {
      "start": 99.26,
      "end": 102.89,
      "text": "changing environments.  On Wrangel, the story looked"
    },
    {
      "start": 102.89,
      "end": 105.09,
      "text": "different. A 2019 isotope study found that the"
    },
    {
      "start": 105.09,
      "end": 110.54,
      "text": "animals' collagen carbon and nitrogen values remained"
    },
    {
      "start": 110.54,
      "end": 112.87,
      "text": "broadly stable across the sampled period."
    },
    {
      "start": 113.26,
      "end": 115.44,
      "text": "That does not prove every season was"
    },
    {
      "start": 115.44,
      "end": 117.36,
      "text": "easy. But it makes the ending a"
    },
    {
      "start": 117.36,
      "end": 119.7,
      "text": "mystery: the signals did not show the"
    },
    {
      "start": 119.7,
      "end": 123.06,
      "text": "clear gradual dietary decline the researchers expected."
    },
    {
      "start": 123.44,
      "end": 126.3,
      "text": "A population survived isolation for millennia."
    },
    {
      "start": 126.71,
      "end": 127.74,
      "text": "And then it disappeared."
    },
    {
      "start": 128.935,
      "end": 130.845,
      "text": "Our first witness is DNA."
    },
    {
      "start": 131.155,
      "end": 135.855,
      "text": "In 2017, researchers compared two woolly mammoth genomes:"
    },
    {
      "start": 136.295,
      "end": 139.515,
      "text": "one from mainland Siberia, around forty five"
    },
    {
      "start": 139.515,
      "end": 142.235,
      "text": "thousand years old, and one from Wrangel"
    },
    {
      "start": 142.235,
      "end": 145.135,
      "text": "Island, around forty three hundred years old."
    },
    {
      "start": 145.455,
      "end": 147.825,
      "text": "The island animal carried an excess of"
    },
    {
      "start": 147.825,
      "end": 150.825,
      "text": "genetic changes that could disrupt genes:"
    },
    {
      "start": 151.285,
      "end": 155.345,
      "text": "more deletions, more deletions affecting genes, and"
    },
    {
      "start": 155.345,
      "end": 157.185,
      "text": "more premature stop signals."
    },
    {
      "start": 157.475,
      "end": 160.135,
      "text": "The researchers interpreted the pattern as consistent"
    },
    {
      "start": 160.425,
      "end": 163.415,
      "text": "with genomic meltdown: in a small population,"
    },
    {
      "start": 163.805,
      "end": 166.675,
      "text": "selection can become less effective at removing"
    },
    {
      "start": 166.675,
      "end": 170.065,
      "text": "harmful variants. The island mammoth's estimated effective"
    },
    {
      "start": 170.065,
      "end": 172.845,
      "text": "population size was more than forty three"
    },
    {
      "start": 172.845,
      "end": 174.865,
      "text": "times lower than the mainland mammoth's."
    },
    {
      "start": 175.275,
      "end": 178.105,
      "text": "Effective population size is a genetic estimate,"
    },
    {
      "start": 178.475,
      "end": 179.945,
      "text": "not a literal headcount."
    },
    {
      "start": 180.375,
      "end": 182.405,
      "text": "This was a striking warning sign."
    },
    {
      "start": 182.855,
      "end": 184.995,
      "text": "But one island genome cannot tell us"
    },
    {
      "start": 184.995,
      "end": 188.295,
      "text": "exactly how every individual lived, or establish"
    },
    {
      "start": 188.295,
      "end": 189.635,
      "text": "the cause of the extinction."
    },
    {
      "start": 190.065,
      "end": 192.815,
      "text": "And one unusual result brought the mystery"
    },
    {
      "start": 192.815,
      "end": 194.435,
      "text": "close to the animal itself."
    },
    {
      "start": 195.623,
      "end": 198.323,
      "text": "The Wrangel genome had two independent loss"
    },
    {
      "start": 198.323,
      "end": 200.753,
      "text": "of function mutations at a gene called"
    },
    {
      "start": 200.753,
      "end": 203.703,
      "text": "FOX Q one. Based on comparisons with"
    },
    {
      "start": 203.703,
      "end": 206.383,
      "text": "other animals, the authors predicted a satin"
    },
    {
      "start": 206.383,
      "end": 208.473,
      "text": "like coat. They did not observe the"
    },
    {
      "start": 208.473,
      "end": 211.353,
      "text": "mammoth's coat directly. A predicted change in"
    },
    {
      "start": 211.353,
      "end": 213.193,
      "text": "hair structure is not proof that the"
    },
    {
      "start": 213.193,
      "end": 215.153,
      "text": "animal lost its wool or froze."
    },
    {
      "start": 215.443,
      "end": 216.543,
      "text": "Think about the difference."
    },
    {
      "start": 216.993,
      "end": 219.503,
      "text": "A single genome can preserve the molecular"
    },
    {
      "start": 219.503,
      "end": 222.123,
      "text": "trace of a possible trait, long after"
    },
    {
      "start": 222.123,
      "end": 223.163,
      "text": "the animal is gone."
    },
    {
      "start": 223.573,
      "end": 225.233,
      "text": "But the trace is not the same"
    },
    {
      "start": 225.233,
      "end": 226.793,
      "text": "as seeing that trait in life."
    },
    {
      "start": 227.263,
      "end": 230.113,
      "text": "That distinction matters throughout this investigation."
    },
    {
      "start": 230.523,
      "end": 234.123,
      "text": "In 2017, the genome offered an important picture"
    },
    {
      "start": 234.123,
      "end": 236.913,
      "text": "of genetic damage. Seven years later, a"
    },
    {
      "start": 236.913,
      "end": 239.253,
      "text": "much larger set of genomes would reveal"
    },
    {
      "start": 239.253,
      "end": 241.543,
      "text": "another part of the same history, and"
    },
    {
      "start": 241.543,
      "end": 243.933,
      "text": "challenge a simple story of a herd"
    },
    {
      "start": 243.933,
      "end": 245.073,
      "text": "slowly collapsing."
    },
    {
      "start": 246.192,
      "end": 248.502,
      "text": "The second witness is chemistry."
    },
    {
      "start": 248.902,
      "end": 252.122,
      "text": "Carbon and nitrogen isotopes in mammoth collagen"
    },
    {
      "start": 252.492,
      "end": 254.042,
      "text": "carry clues about diet."
    },
    {
      "start": 254.492,
      "end": 257.252,
      "text": "Sulfur and strontium can provide clues about"
    },
    {
      "start": 257.252,
      "end": 259.282,
      "text": "water and local geology."
    },
    {
      "start": 259.652,
      "end": 263.932,
      "text": "In 2019, researchers compared samples from Wrangel and"
    },
    {
      "start": 263.932,
      "end": 266.772,
      "text": "other northern regions.  The Wrangel carbon and"
    },
    {
      "start": 266.772,
      "end": 269.222,
      "text": "nitrogen values remained broadly stable in the"
    },
    {
      "start": 269.222,
      "end": 271.832,
      "text": "samples they examined. That is evidence against"
    },
    {
      "start": 271.832,
      "end": 275.092,
      "text": "some kinds of gradual dietary deterioration, not"
    },
    {
      "start": 275.092,
      "end": 276.682,
      "text": "proof the animals were never hungry."
    },
    {
      "start": 277.022,
      "end": 280.392,
      "text": "Other mammoth populations showed different isotopic changes"
    },
    {
      "start": 280.532,
      "end": 283.302,
      "text": "before they disappeared.  The team also found"
    },
    {
      "start": 283.302,
      "end": 286.672,
      "text": "sulfur and strontium patterns consistent with increased"
    },
    {
      "start": 286.672,
      "end": 288.552,
      "text": "bedrock weathering toward the end of the"
    },
    {
      "start": 288.552,
      "end": 292.102,
      "text": "island population's existence. The authors suggested this"
    },
    {
      "start": 292.102,
      "end": 294.032,
      "text": "might have affected drinking water quality."
    },
    {
      "start": 294.442,
      "end": 296.872,
      "text": "It is an interpretation, not a measured"
    },
    {
      "start": 296.872,
      "end": 298.002,
      "text": "glass of bad water."
    },
    {
      "start": 298.462,
      "end": 300.322,
      "text": "Then there is a possible sudden threat:"
    },
    {
      "start": 300.772,
      "end": 303.792,
      "text": "rain falling on snow, freezing into ice,"
    },
    {
      "start": 304.202,
      "end": 306.292,
      "text": "and making plants difficult to reach."
    },
    {
      "start": 306.702,
      "end": 308.992,
      "text": "Such an icing event could damage a"
    },
    {
      "start": 308.992,
      "end": 311.582,
      "text": "small herd quickly. But the study did"
    },
    {
      "start": 311.582,
      "end": 313.222,
      "text": "not witness the fatal winter."
    },
    {
      "start": 313.582,
      "end": 316.222,
      "text": "Ice, water, and genetic strain form a"
    },
    {
      "start": 316.222,
      "end": 319.372,
      "text": "plausible scenario, not a solved case."
    },
    {
      "start": 320.559,
      "end": 322.259,
      "text": "The third witness is us."
    },
    {
      "start": 322.749,
      "end": 325.239,
      "text": "Humans hunted mammoths elsewhere, so it is"
    },
    {
      "start": 325.239,
      "end": 327.579,
      "text": "reasonable to ask whether people reached Wrangel"
    },
    {
      "start": 327.839,
      "end": 329.379,
      "text": "while mammoths were still alive."
    },
    {
      "start": 329.779,
      "end": 332.699,
      "text": "The earliest known archaeological evidence of humans"
    },
    {
      "start": 332.699,
      "end": 334.779,
      "text": "on the island dates to around thirty"
    },
    {
      "start": 334.779,
      "end": 338.319,
      "text": "six hundred years before present, several centuries"
    },
    {
      "start": 338.459,
      "end": 340.399,
      "text": "after the youngest mammoth remains."
    },
    {
      "start": 340.819,
      "end": 343.449,
      "text": "That is the earliest evidence we have,"
    },
    {
      "start": 343.909,
      "end": 345.629,
      "text": "not a perfect record of the first"
    },
    {
      "start": 345.629,
      "end": 349.719,
      "text": "person to arrive. The 2019 researchers said a"
    },
    {
      "start": 349.719,
      "end": 352.749,
      "text": "human contribution cannot be ruled out, because"
    },
    {
      "start": 352.749,
      "end": 355.379,
      "text": "finding direct evidence of an encounter would"
    },
    {
      "start": 355.379,
      "end": 358.729,
      "text": "be difficult.  So the distinction is important."
    },
    {
      "start": 359.169,
      "end": 361.619,
      "text": "Human involvement is possible;"
    },
    {
      "start": 362.139,
      "end": 364.779,
      "text": "the known dates do not establish it."
    },
    {
      "start": 365.029,
      "end": 367.359,
      "text": "The apparent gap is another reason not"
    },
    {
      "start": 367.359,
      "end": 369.289,
      "text": "to turn a suspect into a verdict."
    },
    {
      "start": 370.411,
      "end": 372.861,
      "text": "In 2024, the fourth witness arrived:"
    },
    {
      "start": 372.861,
      "end": 376.431,
      "text": "a study of twenty one Siberian woolly"
    },
    {
      "start": 376.431,
      "end": 379.881,
      "text": "mammoth genomes, including fourteen from the island"
    },
    {
      "start": 379.881,
      "end": 383.351,
      "text": "population and seven earlier mainland animals."
    },
    {
      "start": 383.711,
      "end": 386.451,
      "text": "Together, they gave researchers a much wider"
    },
    {
      "start": 386.451,
      "end": 388.171,
      "text": "window into the genetic history."
    },
    {
      "start": 388.481,
      "end": 389.741,
      "text": "The bottleneck was real."
    },
    {
      "start": 390.201,
      "end": 394.181,
      "text": "One measure of genetic diversity, heterozygosity, fell"
    },
    {
      "start": 394.181,
      "end": 396.881,
      "text": "by more than forty percent after isolation."
    },
    {
      "start": 397.211,
      "end": 400.321,
      "text": "Long runs of homozygosity, stretches where an"
    },
    {
      "start": 400.321,
      "end": 404.021,
      "text": "animal carries matching inherited copies, increased from"
    },
    {
      "start": 404.021,
      "end": 405.931,
      "text": "roughly ten to forty two percent of"
    },
    {
      "start": 405.931,
      "end": 409.631,
      "text": "the genome. Diversity in the major histocompatibility"
    },
    {
      "start": 409.631,
      "end": 412.431,
      "text": "complex, a group of genes involved in"
    },
    {
      "start": 412.431,
      "end": 415.701,
      "text": "immune responses, fell more than genome-wide"
    },
    {
      "start": 415.701,
      "end": 418.621,
      "text": "diversity.  Those are serious genetic changes."
    },
    {
      "start": 419.061,
      "end": 421.361,
      "text": "But a different signal complicated the story."
    },
    {
      "start": 421.851,
      "end": 425.451,
      "text": "Modelling suggested that effective population size dropped"
    },
    {
      "start": 425.451,
      "end": 427.481,
      "text": "to eight or fewer at the bottleneck,"
    },
    {
      "start": 427.881,
      "end": 430.191,
      "text": "then recovered to around two hundred to"
    },
    {
      "start": 430.191,
      "end": 433.351,
      "text": "three hundred within roughly twenty generations."
    },
    {
      "start": 433.781,
      "end": 436.601,
      "text": "Again, that is an effective genetic population"
    },
    {
      "start": 436.601,
      "end": 439.521,
      "text": "size, not a count of individual mammoths."
    },
    {
      "start": 439.911,
      "end": 442.931,
      "text": "The population appeared comparatively stable across the"
    },
    {
      "start": 442.931,
      "end": 445.021,
      "text": "period represented by the samples."
    },
    {
      "start": 446.108,
      "end": 448.778,
      "text": "Recovery did not erase the genetic consequences"
    },
    {
      "start": 448.778,
      "end": 453.448,
      "text": "of isolation. The 2024 researchers looked at predicted"
    },
    {
      "start": 453.448,
      "end": 457.008,
      "text": "harmful mutations, taking care with a technical"
    },
    {
      "start": 457.008,
      "end": 459.798,
      "text": "problem: genomes differ in how much of"
    },
    {
      "start": 459.798,
      "end": 461.268,
      "text": "their sequence can be read."
    },
    {
      "start": 461.728,
      "end": 464.698,
      "text": "Imagine comparing damage in two rooms through"
    },
    {
      "start": 464.698,
      "end": 466.298,
      "text": "windows of different sizes."
    },
    {
      "start": 466.778,
      "end": 468.528,
      "text": "A bigger window lets you see more,"
    },
    {
      "start": 468.998,
      "end": 471.138,
      "text": "even when the rooms are equally damaged."
    },
    {
      "start": 471.408,
      "end": 473.848,
      "text": "After accounting for coverage and data quality,"
    },
    {
      "start": 474.308,
      "end": 476.488,
      "text": "the team found two opposing trends."
    },
    {
      "start": 476.758,
      "end": 479.028,
      "text": "Variants predicted to have the highest impact"
    },
    {
      "start": 479.028,
      "end": 482.108,
      "text": "became less common, consistent with selection purging"
    },
    {
      "start": 482.108,
      "end": 485.828,
      "text": "some of them. Meanwhile, moderately harmful variants"
    },
    {
      "start": 485.828,
      "end": 489.898,
      "text": "accumulated, consistent with genetic drift outpacing selection."
    },
    {
      "start": 490.368,
      "end": 492.618,
      "text": "These are predictions about effects, not a"
    },
    {
      "start": 492.618,
      "end": 494.958,
      "text": "direct medical examination of each mammoth."
    },
    {
      "start": 495.358,
      "end": 497.618,
      "text": "Across the sampled history, the team did"
    },
    {
      "start": 497.618,
      "end": 500.728,
      "text": "not see a clear, accelerating genomic collapse."
    },
    {
      "start": 501.108,
      "end": 503.668,
      "text": "But their youngest genome predates the final"
    },
    {
      "start": 503.668,
      "end": 507.508,
      "text": "generations. Demographic recovery and long-lasting genetic"
    },
    {
      "start": 507.508,
      "end": 511.278,
      "text": "strain can coexist. Neither finding, on its"
    },
    {
      "start": 511.278,
      "end": 513.468,
      "text": "own, names what killed the herd."
    },
    {
      "start": 514.602,
      "end": 516.032,
      "text": "Here is the missing witness."
    },
    {
      "start": 516.542,
      "end": 520.452,
      "text": "The 2024 genomic study had no samples from"
    },
    {
      "start": 520.452,
      "end": 524.022,
      "text": "the population's final ten generations, roughly three"
    },
    {
      "start": 524.022,
      "end": 527.242,
      "text": "centuries. Its youngest genome was dated to"
    },
    {
      "start": 527.242,
      "end": 530.272,
      "text": "around forty three hundred calibrated years before"
    },
    {
      "start": 530.272,
      "end": 533.222,
      "text": "present. That gap applies to the genome"
    },
    {
      "start": 533.222,
      "end": 535.722,
      "text": "dataset; it does not mean there is"
    },
    {
      "start": 535.722,
      "end": 537.432,
      "text": "no other evidence from the period."
    },
    {
      "start": 537.932,
      "end": 539.492,
      "text": "We can study the long setup."
    },
    {
      "start": 539.922,
      "end": 542.102,
      "text": "We cannot read a complete genetic record"
    },
    {
      "start": 542.102,
      "end": 543.132,
      "text": "of the final chapter."
    },
    {
      "start": 543.562,
      "end": 545.322,
      "text": "There is also a newer kind of"
    },
    {
      "start": 545.322,
      "end": 550.312,
      "text": "lead. In 2025, researchers studied ancient host-associated"
    },
    {
      "start": 550.312,
      "end": 554.012,
      "text": "microbial DNA across hundreds of mammoth specimens,"
    },
    {
      "start": 554.432,
      "end": 556.862,
      "text": "including material far older than the Wrangel"
    },
    {
      "start": 556.862,
      "end": 560.192,
      "text": "population. Some bacteria were related to known"
    },
    {
      "start": 560.192,
      "end": 563.652,
      "text": "pathogens. But related does not mean responsible."
    },
    {
      "start": 564.062,
      "end": 566.482,
      "text": "The study does not identify a disease"
    },
    {
      "start": 566.632,
      "end": 569.182,
      "text": "that killed the Wrangel mammoths, and any"
    },
    {
      "start": 569.182,
      "end": 570.952,
      "text": "health effects remain uncertain."
    },
    {
      "start": 571.362,
      "end": 573.032,
      "text": "The value of this research is the"
    },
    {
      "start": 573.032,
      "end": 576.502,
      "text": "question it opens: what can carefully authenticated"
    },
    {
      "start": 576.502,
      "end": 579.512,
      "text": "traces of microbes tell us alongside the"
    },
    {
      "start": 579.512,
      "end": 583.102,
      "text": "animal's own DNA? For now, the diagnosis"
    },
    {
      "start": 583.102,
      "end": 583.992,
      "text": "is still missing."
    },
    {
      "start": 585.141,
      "end": 586.691,
      "text": "So what can we actually say?"
    },
    {
      "start": 587.181,
      "end": 591.241,
      "text": "Three columns.  Supported: the Wrangel population went"
    },
    {
      "start": 591.241,
      "end": 592.671,
      "text": "through a severe bottleneck."
    },
    {
      "start": 593.071,
      "end": 596.331,
      "text": "The sampled genomes show reduced diversity and"
    },
    {
      "start": 596.331,
      "end": 600.371,
      "text": "increased homozygosity, followed by a modelled demographic"
    },
    {
      "start": 600.371,
      "end": 602.981,
      "text": "recovery. Genetic strain persisted."
    },
    {
      "start": 603.451,
      "end": 606.281,
      "text": "Isotope patterns were broadly stable in important"
    },
    {
      "start": 606.281,
      "end": 609.751,
      "text": "dietary indicators, while other signals were interpreted"
    },
    {
      "start": 609.751,
      "end": 612.031,
      "text": "as possible changes in water quality."
    },
    {
      "start": 612.311,
      "end": 616.091,
      "text": "Plausible, not proven: a severe icing event,"
    },
    {
      "start": 616.531,
      "end": 620.901,
      "text": "disease, poorer water, human involvement, or some"
    },
    {
      "start": 620.901,
      "end": 624.401,
      "text": "combination of pressures affecting a small isolated"
    },
    {
      "start": 624.401,
      "end": 627.501,
      "text": "population. Each requires evidence we do not"
    },
    {
      "start": 627.501,
      "end": 629.581,
      "text": "yet have.  Not established:"
    },
    {
      "start": 630.011,
      "end": 632.711,
      "text": "a single named killer, a fatal winter"
    },
    {
      "start": 632.711,
      "end": 635.271,
      "text": "directly recorded in the bones, or a"
    },
    {
      "start": 635.271,
      "end": 637.131,
      "text": "genetic test proving the cause."
    },
    {
      "start": 637.501,
      "end": 640.111,
      "text": "The later genomic study challenges a simple"
    },
    {
      "start": 640.111,
      "end": 643.631,
      "text": "account of inexorable collapse, but cannot tell"
    },
    {
      "start": 643.631,
      "end": 645.541,
      "text": "us what happened in the missing final"
    },
    {
      "start": 645.541,
      "end": 648.891,
      "text": "generations.  These categories are not rivals."
    },
    {
      "start": 649.311,
      "end": 651.991,
      "text": "A vulnerable population and a sudden event"
    },
    {
      "start": 652.341,
      "end": 654.801,
      "text": "could work together. That is a hypothesis"
    },
    {
      "start": 654.801,
      "end": 657.511,
      "text": "about compounding risks, not the answer to"
    },
    {
      "start": 657.511,
      "end": 658.841,
      "text": "this particular case."
    },
    {
      "start": 660.031,
      "end": 662.101,
      "text": "Each witness tells us something different."
    },
    {
      "start": 662.481,
      "end": 665.811,
      "text": "The 2017 genome revealed potential genetic damage."
    },
    {
      "start": 665.811,
      "end": 668.741,
      "text": "The isotope record offered a picture of"
    },
    {
      "start": 668.741,
      "end": 671.661,
      "text": "stable dietary signals, with a possible warning"
    },
    {
      "start": 671.661,
      "end": 674.621,
      "text": "about water. Archaeology gives us the earliest"
    },
    {
      "start": 674.621,
      "end": 677.071,
      "text": "known evidence of humans, not a complete"
    },
    {
      "start": 677.071,
      "end": 681.751,
      "text": "attendance list. The 2024 genomes suggest that population"
    },
    {
      "start": 681.751,
      "end": 684.541,
      "text": "recovery and genetic strain lasted together for"
    },
    {
      "start": 684.541,
      "end": 687.051,
      "text": "thousands of years.  The mistake would be"
    },
    {
      "start": 687.051,
      "end": 688.871,
      "text": "to pick the most dramatic clue and"
    },
    {
      "start": 688.871,
      "end": 690.531,
      "text": "declare the mystery solved."
    },
    {
      "start": 690.811,
      "end": 693.451,
      "text": "A small gene pool, a changing environment,"
    },
    {
      "start": 693.891,
      "end": 695.991,
      "text": "and an unlucky season might interact."
    },
    {
      "start": 696.701,
      "end": 698.621,
      "text": "But a plausible story is not the"
    },
    {
      "start": 698.621,
      "end": 699.851,
      "text": "same thing as proof."
    },
    {
      "start": 700.251,
      "end": 703.101,
      "text": "The same distinction matters for living populations"
    },
    {
      "start": 703.101,
      "end": 705.191,
      "text": "that are small and isolated today."
    },
    {
      "start": 705.581,
      "end": 708.451,
      "text": "A rebound in numbers can be encouraging"
    },
    {
      "start": 708.451,
      "end": 710.601,
      "text": "without erasing every genetic risk."
    },
    {
      "start": 710.831,
      "end": 714.181,
      "text": "Protecting connections between populations may help give"
    },
    {
      "start": 714.181,
      "end": 716.371,
      "text": "them more options when conditions change."
    },
    {
      "start": 716.791,
      "end": 719.221,
      "text": "For the last Wrangel mammoths, the ending"
    },
    {
      "start": 719.221,
      "end": 720.851,
      "text": "remains a gap in the file."
    },
    {
      "start": 721.341,
      "end": 723.181,
      "text": "We know more about the long journey"
    },
    {
      "start": 723.501,
      "end": 724.541,
      "text": "than the final moment."
    },
    {
      "start": 724.851,
      "end": 726.571,
      "text": "And the last question is not just"
    },
    {
      "start": 726.571,
      "end": 728.891,
      "text": "what killed them. It is what evidence"
    },
    {
      "start": 728.891,
      "end": 729.901,
      "text": "we are still missing."
    }
  ],
  "caption_method": "PocketSphinx forced alignment against known transcript; automatic timing estimates",
  "visual_provenance": "AI-generated background illustrations, original procedural three-dimensional graphics and the earlier procedural 3D opening."
}
